tools/binutils-2.10-ee.patch: the Emotion Engine and DVP pieces the period
linker needs, for GNU binutils 2.10 (ftp.gnu.org, GPL-2.0-or-later).

A backport to 2.10's single bfd/elf32-mips.c of the matching hunks of
ps2dev's binutils-2.14-PS2.patch (github.com/ps2dev/ps2toolchain, commit
aa984e7, patches/binutils-2.14-PS2.patch; there they sit in
bfd/elfxx-mips.c, bfd/cpu-mips.c, bfd/archures.c, bfd/bfd-in2.h and
include/elf/mips.h), limited to what the ICO link measures:

 - the R5900 machine: bfd_mach_mips5900 and E_MIPS_MACH_5900, so the
   inputs' e_flags mach bits (0x00920000) survive into the output instead
   of being rewritten to the plain MIPS III value;
 - the DVP overlay sections dvp-as writes: SHT_DVP_OVERLAY_TABLE
   (.DVP.ovlytab, entsize 12, sh_link to .DVP.ovlystrtab set in
   final_write_processing), .DVP.ovlystrtab as SHT_STRTAB and the
   .DVP.overlay.* SHT_DVP_OVERLAY sections, read and written by type.

Applied by tools/setup.sh with `patch -p1` in the extracted binutils-2.10
tree. Nothing here comes from an SDK.

